    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/university-controller-26": {
      "title": "University Controller/Director of Fiscal Affairs",
      "description": "University Controller/Director of Fiscal Affairs | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content × Microsoft is experiencing a widespread outage affecting Outlook and other services, including Microsoft 365, Teams, SharePoint, OneDrive, and Copilot. Some university services may be disrupted. Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Controller/Director of Fiscal Affairs Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Controller/Director of Fiscal Affairs Rank: Administrator VII Search #: S26-014 Job Posted: November 11, 2026 Southern Connecticut State University is a diverse and student-centered university dedicated to academic excellence, access, and service for the public good. Southern provides a supportive and welcoming environment for all members of its community through a campus wide commitment to social justice.  Founded as a teacher’s college in 1893, Southern has evolved over the past century into a comprehensive public university of more than 8,500 students, offering graduate and undergraduate programs in the liberal arts and professional disciplines. It is one of four universities in the Connecticut State Colleges and Universities System. The University is located in New Haven, a city rich with arts and culture, and less than 90 miles from New York City and 140 miles from Boston. Reporting to the Executive Vice President for Finance and Administration, the Controller/Director of Fiscal Affairs directs the University's fiscal services, fiscal reporting, analysis, projections and planning, including budget development, monitoring and control. Serves as the Chief Fiscal Officer of the University in the absence of the Executive Vice President for Finance and Administration, and as a key liaison to the CSCU system office, auditors, and regulatory agencies on matters pertaining to the finances of the university. Position Responsibilities: Leads the staff and operations of the University's business and financial management functions; including budget preparation and management, accounting, and financial reporting, analysis and control. Supervises the operations of Accounting, Accounts Payable, Grants Administration, Financial Planning, Student Accounts (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering), Purchasing, Payroll, Card Office and other related functions. This includes supervision and evaluation of staff in these areas. Develops and implements financial reporting and control systems and procedures to ensure effective and appropriate tracking, management, and reporting on revenues, expenses, treasury and cash flow matters, assets, liabilities, and property. Develops, implements and evaluates fiscal policies to ensure appropriate financial oversight of the university. Represents the University to external agencies, the CSCU System office, state and other auditors to facilitate the administration of the University's financial planning and control responsibilities; keeps current with legislative developments, GASB and GAAP rules, federal regulations pertaining to higher education finance, system and university policies and procedures, and other changes that impact the University's fiscal and business operations. Reviews existing programs and procedures to identify trends, more efficient and cost effective methods of operations, and to assure that expenditures track the strategic and tactical goals and objectives of the university. Prepares a wide variety of financial and analytical reports, including the annual financial statements, to provide current information on the University's financial status; information used in long range planning, contract negotiations, staffing needs and related operational decisions. Works with external auditors in the preparation of audit reports for State agencies, Federal government, and the NCAA; responds to audit findings; identifies and implements corrective policies and practices if needed. Performs other duties and responsibilities related to those enumerated above that do not alter the basic level of responsibility of the position. Qualifications: A CPA, MBA or Master's degree in Accounting, Finance, or equivalent is required. Seven years of progressively more responsible experience in Financial Management in Higher Education, public or private, including the development and implementation of effective financial systems, controls, reporting, and analysis. Demonstrated ability to plan and develop sound financial reporting systems; ability to interpret and administer federal laws and regulations, payroll, purchasing, grant administration and contract administration procedures; demonstrated effective interpersonal skills and strong oral and written communications skills required. Proven skills in leadership, management, promoting and managing change, team building, collaboration, and creating, communicating, managing and extracting broad organizational value from complex financial data and plans. These qualifications may be waived for individuals with appropriate alternate experience. Application: For full consideration, please submit a letter of interest, resume and contact information for three professional references to finsearch1@southernct.edu . For full consideration, please submit application materials no later than December 11, 2026.  The position will remain open until filled. Southern Connecticut State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. The University seeks to enhance the diversity of its faculty and staff. People of color, women, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-early-college-26": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant - SCSU Early College | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content × Microsoft is experiencing a widespread outage affecting Outlook and other services, including Microsoft 365, Teams, SharePoint, OneDrive, and Copilot. Some university services may be disrupted. Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant - SCSU Early College Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Assistant - SCSU Early College Start date: November 30, 2026 This is a part-time position, which may be renewed at the discretion of the University. University Assistant appointments may be for up to one (1) year in length. Hours/Week: The UA is expected to work up to 19 hours per week. The exact schedule will be established between the Supervisor and the successful applicant to meet the needs of the department. Position Justification SCSU Early College is seeking an energetic and self-motivated University Assistant (UA) to provide project management, directed research, promotional outreach, and event planning for a wide variety of initiatives in our department. Preferred Qualifications, Experience, Requirements B.S./B.A. degree required. Must possess strong written and verbal communication skills, creative problem-solving skills, and an ability to lead high-level group projects with limited supervision in a tactful, strategic, and professional manner. UA should be well versed in Microsoft Office 365 Suite. Prior experience with project management and business communication in a professional corporate or educational setting is strongly preferred. The UA must be available to work on campus 19 hours per week (Monday-Friday) between the hours of 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Hours are flexible. Position Responsibilities: Assist in daily communications and office operations Assist coordinating and conducting Early College information sessions and tours with partnering school districts Assist in fielding questions from Early College K-12 partners, students, and parents Coordinate communications to partners, department chairs, and faculty liaisons Assist with coordination of professional development programs and orientations Assist with the design, development, and marketing of SCSU Early College for schools, teachers, families, and community organizations, including promotional outreach strategies Assist with program accreditation document preparation and coordination Contribute to the efficient and accurate registration of students Be prepared to work with new dual enrollment management system. Depending on experience and credentials, the hourly wage range is $15-20/hour. Individuals with specialized skills or training or holding advanced degrees will be paid at the higher end of the hourly range. Qualified applicants should send a cover letter, resume, and list of three references to earlycollege@southernct.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    }
  },
